# bugs.json is COMMITTED, deliberately. It is derived rather than source, which
# normally argues for ignoring it, but it is also the register itself: a clone
# without it is a page with nothing to draw, and the point of publishing this is
# that the state of the work is checkable by anyone.
#
# What that publishes is bounded and enforced, not assumed. A Vulnerable row —
# the great majority — carries an opaque bug id and a fingerprint of its report
# and nothing else: no path, no function, no description, no crash text, no
# reproducer. extract.py's check_published() refuses to write a row carrying
# more, and refuses a Vulnerable value that is not an opaque digest, so it holds
# on every extraction rather than having been reviewed once. Processing and
# Patched rows carry titles, message-ids, diffs and CVE numbers already public
# on lore and in the kernel's own history.
#
# The half-written file the extractor renames over is not source at all.
bugs.json.tmp

# Credentials and keys. Nothing here needs any today; these patterns exist so
# that an .env or a key dropped in during debugging cannot be committed by a
# reflexive `git add -A`.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.token
*_token
*.secret
secrets.*
credentials.*
.netrc
.htpasswd
service-account*.json

# Logs — they record the IPs of everyone who visited.
*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Static build for GitHub Pages. Assembled by build.py from web/ and bugs.json,
# so it is derived rather than source — and it contains a copy of bugs.json,
# which is ignored right above for good reason. Publishing means adding it
# deliberately with `git add -f docs`, which is the point.
docs/

# What reproduction/repro.sh --host writes where it is run from, which is
# normally a checkout of this repository: one shared kernel object store and
# the 650MB kernelCTF image in .cache/, and a directory per bug holding its
# published files, a kernel checkout and a bzImage. All of it is derived, and
# all of it is measured in gigabytes. The directory names are bug ids -- 16 hex
# characters, and the same again with -latest for a build against mainline.
.cache/
/[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]/
/[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]-latest/
